"display_date": "2023-11-22T11:45:33.948Z",
"excerpt": {
"text": "Another Thanksgiving, another case study in the complex relationship between gratitude and discontent in America. In many respects, a typical U.S. family’s cup runneth over, especially relative to the situations facing families in places such as Ukraine, Gaza, Israel, Venezuela, Afghanistan — the list of poor, oppressed or war-torn nations is long. Macroeconomic data indicate that unemployment is hovering near all-time lows, that inflation is coming down, possibly without a recession, and that real wages have recently resumed their growth."
